BB-1-3-013:
Factor the three inequalities in \(y = f(x)\): (1) \((y - 3)\left( y^{2} - 2y + 4 \right) \geq 0 \Rightarrow y \geq 3\) (since \(y^{2} - 2y + 4 = (y - 1)^{2} + 3 > 0\));
(2) \((y - 1)(y - 3) \geq 0 \Rightarrow y \leq 1\) or \(y \geq 3\);
(3) \((y - 2)(y - 3) \leq 0 \Rightarrow 2 \leq y \leq 3\).
The intersection of \(y \geq 3\), \(\left( y \leq 1\text{ or }y \geq 3 \right)\), and \(2 \leq y \leq 3\) is the single value \(f(x) = 3\ \forall x \in R\)!
Since \(b_{1},b_{2},b_{3}\) are in G.P., \(\ln b_{1},\ln b_{2},\ln b_{3}\) are in A.P., and adding the constant \(f(k) = 3\) to each term gives \(3 + \ln b_{1},3 + \ln b_{2},3 + \ln b_{3}\), which are also in A.P.

